      "Title": "Exam C2150-624 topic 1 question 7 discussion - ExamTopics",
      "Question": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "An Administrator working with IBM Security QRadar SIEM V7.2.8 needs to delete a single value named User1 from a reference set with the name \"Allowed Users\" from the command line interface."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Which command will accomplish this?"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Choices": {
        "A": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A. ./UtilReferenceSet.sh purge \"Allowed Users\" User1"
            }
          ]
        },
        "B": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "B. ./ReferenceSetUtil.sh purge \"Allowed Users\" User1"
            }
          ]
        },
        "C": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "C. ./ReferenceSetUtil.sh delete \"Allowed\\ Users\" User1"
            }
          ]
        },
        "D": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "D. ./UtilReferenceSet.sh delete \"Allowed\\ Users\" User1"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "Answer": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Suggested Answer: B \ud83d\uddf3\ufe0f"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "The Referencesetutil.sh purge is the correct syntax of the command. It deletes the specific user when you mention it within the reference set."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Reference -"
